{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1028974-how-to-place-the-hallow-ones-in-a-game","id":1028974,"title":"How to place the Hallow Ones in a game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-09T05:20:24-08:00","id":1028974,"title":"How to place the Hallow Ones in a game.","content":"In my game, that is a mixed game, Mages are few in the city for various reasons. In fact there will be one that is sort of a watcher type and five of them that are a clique of sorts.I want the five to be Hollow Ones like in the first edition. So my question is what would they be? Are they Free Counsel that just have a unique name or are they a Legacies or some other such thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T05:50:20-08:00","id":1028984,"title":"","content":"Hollow Ones aren't in 1st Edition, that's Ascension. There's an Ascension to Awakening translation guide on th forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T05:51:25-08:00","id":1028985,"title":"","content":"The only faction called Hollow Ones I recall are from <b>Mage the Ascension</b>, not <b>Mage the Awakening</b>. The two are completely different games, and this forum is for the latter. Were you meaning to post this in the Ascension forums, or did you mistake Ascension for Awakening 1E?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T06:46:31-08:00","id":1029020,"title":"","content":"I misspoke. I meant Mage the Ascension. The reason I posted here, and not in the Classic forum is because I thought there would be people more able to answer the question seeing as it's a forum on Mage the Awakening and the question pertains to that rule set. Clear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:01:05-08:00","id":1029027,"title":"","content":"In that case, the closest equivalent would be a Legacy that mirrors their philosophy and practices. However, you'd have to narrow down the concept, because Legacies in general are more thematically tight-packed than the Traditions/Crafts/Conventions are. Perhaps you'd have better luck in the homebrew Legacies thread.<br /> <br /> Hmm... my suggestion would be having Decadent and/or Nihilistic Romanticism as the Legacy's theme, with the modern members incorporating modern punk stuff, pulpy fiction and subculture in general, something that might not settle well with the elders and traditionalists. Oblations would be around indulging themselves in the aforementioned cultures, while Yantras would be exalting their worth in public and snipping quotes from the literary and fiction works of those cultures. They'd have Moros as their parent Path, reflecting the Path's tendency towards promoting change and entropy in general, and the Free Council as their primary Order. The third Ruling Arcanum can be Fate, with Attainments based on reenacting tropes in Romantic literature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:58:27-08:00","id":1029813,"title":"","content":"Whether you choose to use a homebrew Legacy or not, the Hollow Ones could easily be depicted as a Nameless Order, either one that has joined with the Free Council or one that remains independent and likely marginalized. The thing to remember about the Free Council is that it's not just another Order, its a diverse sect in and of itself, formed from numerous disparate magical traditions organized around a relatively loose set of principles. Members of the Free Council include DJs who seek supernal resonances in popular music, morally ambiguous sorcerers drawing on the Haitian Vodou tradition, eccentric physicists who integrate supernal truths with quantum mechanics, storytellers and spirit-talkers from marginalized traditional cultures, radical talk radio hosts trying to goad sleepers toward Awakening, and alchemists seeking self-perfection through physical crafts. <br /> <br /> In terms of Ascension, it's my impression that members of the Dreamspeakers, the Sons of Ether, the Hollow Ones, the Verbena, and the Virtual Adepts could fit fairly comfortably into the Free Council, though really members of any number of traditions and crafts might, to the extent that they reflect magical beliefs from sleeper cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T16:04:08-08:00","id":1029814,"title":"","content":"Really looks like they'd just be Free Council.<br /> <br /> If not, you could make them Orderless. Considering how open the Free Council is, it's easy to justify them being members, even if all they offer is lip service to the cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-10-2017, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T04:22:50-08:00","id":1029996,"title":"","content":"thanks guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:52:37-08:00","id":1030291,"title":"","content":"Hollow Ones in 2e Mate are something very different, they're sleepwalkers that hold 5 mana that causes, their memories to reset, when they run out amoung other traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T22:00:40-08:00","id":1030437,"title":"","content":"No reason that an unrelated group couldn't also use the name. I think the name was suppsoed to be a TS Elliot reference, but modified to be gender neutral, rather than referring to any specific spiritual emptiness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}